    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a27">

                <pb facs="0289" n="217" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg217"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 26 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brooks to Mr.
                            Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Queenstown</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21</hi>,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have recently had several personal
                    applications from friends of Mr. Henry O’Mahoney (political prisoner now in Her
                    Majesty’s jail at Limerick, and claiming to <pb facs="0290" n="218"
                        xml:id="pg218"/> be an American citizen) for information regarding the
                    result of his application through me for your intervention in his behalf. To
                    these inquiries I have replied, promising to communicate with you again.</p>
                <p>O’Mahoney himself has written to me, giving a brief supplementary statement, in
                    effect that he is desirous of going back to America for the purpose of engaging
                    in the exportation of apples and other fruits to this country.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. P. BROOKS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul,
                        &amp;c.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
